{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2836 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "4ebb30cfd6fa88a02a7f83694dfda4433d74bfc16e9d32f43d6667cb38774af6" :edb/db-before-t 2835 :edb/db-after-t 2836 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536148 50 #inst "2026-10-09T16:59:05.883Z" 13194139536148 true] [17592186119661 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386086 13194139536148 true] [17592186119663 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386093 13194139536148 true] [17592186386086 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386087 13194139536148 true] [17592186386086 1089 "q-33135" 13194139536148 true] [17592186386086 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536148 true] [17592186386086 1100 "What is the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)=⟨4t,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩$ at the point $P(4,0,1)?$" 13194139536148 true] [17592186386086 1113 #uuid "8e40fe88-bf16-5d89-9381-2099d0c7a194" 13194139536148 true] [17592186386086 1145 "For a curve $r(t)=⟨x(t),y(t),z(t)⟩$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the value of $t$ that corresponds to the point $P(4,0,1)$ on the given curve. We know that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =⟨4,\\,0,\\,1⟩ \\\\ ⟨4t,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡t,\\,{t}^{2}⟩ & =⟨4,\\,0,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the respective components gives the system\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}4t=4 \\\\ 4\\operatorname{ln}⁡t=0 \\\\ {t}^{2}=1.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equality, $t=1.$ This value satisfies the other two equations. Therefore, the point $P(4,0,1)$ is at the tip of $r(1).$  \n\nNow, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(4\\operatorname{ln}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,\\frac{4}{t},\\,2t⟩ \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =⟨4,\\,\\frac{4}{(1)},\\,2(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,\\,4,\\,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}^{′}(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(1)$ and obtain the unit tangent vector to the given curve at $P(4,0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(1)}{‖{r}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}⟨4,\\,4,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536148 true] [17592186386087 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386088 13194139536148 true] [17592186386087 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386089 13194139536148 true] [17592186386087 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386090 13194139536148 true] [17592186386087 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386091 13194139536148 true] [17592186386087 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386092 13194139536148 true] [17592186386087 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536148 true] [17592186386087 1041 "selection" 13194139536148 true] [17592186386087 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386090 13194139536148 true] [17592186386087 1110 #uuid "19921ccc-8653-514b-b4e2-8903d06eeea3" 13194139536148 true] [17592186386088 1034 "⟨\\frac{2}{5},\\,\\frac{1}{5},\\,\\frac{1}{5}⟩" 13194139536148 true] [17592186386088 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536148 true] [17592186386088 1111 #uuid "a1d5bb41-39a5-5021-9fcf-ec76b5a441e1" 13194139536148 true] [17592186386089 1034 "⟨\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}⟩" 13194139536148 true] [17592186386089 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536148 true] [17592186386089 1111 #uuid "11b36f08-4bb8-5cfb-9bd8-7c889f1be15d" 13194139536148 true] [17592186386090 1034 "⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3}⟩" 13194139536148 true] [17592186386090 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536148 true] [17592186386090 1111 #uuid "a1306070-27b8-54f8-999c-180f53d0f08e" 13194139536148 true] [17592186386091 1034 "⟨\\frac{2}{3},\\,\\frac{1}{3},\\,\\frac{2}{3}⟩" 13194139536148 true] [17592186386091 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536148 true] [17592186386091 1111 #uuid "2d0d0109-8947-568a-8e09-9c03bddda6e3" 13194139536148 true] [17592186386092 1034 "⟨\\frac{1}{5},\\,\\frac{2}{5},\\,\\frac{2}{5}⟩" 13194139536148 true] [17592186386092 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536148 true] [17592186386092 1111 #uuid "b55dd1b5-bd81-5a92-b705-9806ff8f75f5" 13194139536148 true] [17592186386093 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386094 13194139536148 true] [17592186386093 1089 "q-64492" 13194139536148 true] [17592186386093 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536148 true] [17592186386093 1100 "Find the unit tangent vector to the curve $r(t)={t}^{2}p(t)$ at the point corresponding to $t=1$, given that  $p(1)=i-\\,j-k\\,$ and $\\,{p}^{′}(1)=-i+\\,j+\\,k.$" 13194139536148 true] [17592186386093 1113 #uuid "5c9414af-cb9d-5103-8118-a585c41e78a4" 13194139536148 true] [17592186386093 1145 "For a curve $r(t)=x(t)i+y(t)j+z(t)k$, the unit tangent vector $T(t)$ at the point $P(x(t),y(t),z(t))$ is given by\n\n$$\nT(t)=\\frac{{r}^{′}(t)}{‖{r}^{′}(t)‖}\n$$\n\nFirst, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and evaluate it at $t=1:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}p(t)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2})\\cdot p(t)+{t}^{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(p(t)) \\\\  & =2t\\,p(t)+{t}^{2}\\,{p}^{′}(t) \\\\ {r}^{′}(1) & =2(1)\\,p(1)+(1)^{2}\\,{p}^{′}(1) \\\\  & =2(i-\\,j-k)+(-i+\\,j+\\,k) \\\\  & =2i-2\\,j-2k-i+j+\\,k \\\\  & =i-j-k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the magnitude of ${r}^{′}(1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖r(1)‖ & =\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we normalize ${r}^{′}(1):$  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1) & =\\frac{{r}^{′}(1)}{‖{r}^{′}(1)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot (i-j-k) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}(i-j-k)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the unit tangent vector to the curve at the point that corresponds to $t=1$ is  $T(1)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}(i-j-k).$" 13194139536148 true] [17592186386094 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386095 13194139536148 true] [17592186386094 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386096 13194139536148 true] [17592186386094 1000 #edb/r